                    insight_bankable:       `Bankable-only trap: you funded the corridors private capital would have built anyway and deferred the isolated-province project with the highest social return. Aggregate IRR looks strong, but the public co-financing added almost no additionality — and the province that most needed it got nothing.`,
                    insight_forecast:       `Renegotiation cycle repeated: you regulated the tariff and the investor IRR on a demand forecast above the independent study. When traffic comes in at the credible number, revenue misses and the concessionaire returns for amendment — exactly the failure mode ARIC was created to stop.`,
                    insight_guarantee:      `Treasury blank cheque: you made the projects investable with uncapped minimum-revenue guarantees. The liability is off the budget line but firmly on the country’s balance sheet — a present-value contingent exposure of roughly S/ 600M if demand disappoints, unpriced and unbounded.`,
